WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.599 --> 00:00:03.389
Natasha: What’d you get for question #2?

00:00:03.389 --> 00:00:05.980
Cause I think it’s-
Hanson, could you stay awake and at least

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.059
pretend like you’re trying to pass
tomorrow’s test?

00:00:08.059 --> 00:00:09.559
Hanson: Dunno, ask Derek?

00:00:09.559 --> 00:00:10.559
Derek?

00:00:10.559 --> 00:00:11.559
Derek: Depression?

00:00:11.559 --> 00:00:15.160
What even is depression-
Natasha: Depression, major depressive disorder,

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.060
or clinical depression, is a mood
disorder that causes a prolonged feeling of

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:22.780
sadness affecting more than 264 million
people worldwide.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:27.199
Natasha: It is associated with decreased activity
of serotonin, a neurotransmitter in the

00:00:27.199 --> 00:00:30.230
central nervous system responsible for feelings
of happiness.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:33.900
Hanson: When the presynaptic cell receives
stimulus and transfers an impulse - (action

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:37.499
potential) - down the neuron's axon, membrane
vesicles containing neurotransmitters

00:00:37.499 --> 00:00:38.640
release serotonin.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:42.190
Derek: Serotonin travels through the synaptic
cleft and binds to 5-HT receptors on the

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:46.170
spines of postsynaptic neurons, which depolarizes
them, allowing for the rapid

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:49.699
continuation of impulses that induce feelings
of happiness.

00:00:49.699 --> 00:00:52.940
After being released,
neurotransmitters are absorbed into the presynaptic

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.390
neuron where they are either reused
or decomposed.

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:58.949
Derek: Depression disrupts this process, preventing
the generation of "happy feelings."

00:00:58.949 --> 00:01:01.760
Hanson: SSRI (Selective serotonin reuptake
inhibitors) are drugs that block the serotonin

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.820
transporter causing serotonin to be in the
synaptic cleft for longer periods of time,

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:10.530
additionally stimulating the 5-HT receptors
and restoring serotonin levels during action

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:15.469
potentials to near-homeostatic standards,
allowing patients to feel “normal” again,

00:01:15.469 --> 00:01:16.939
for the
duration of the drug.

00:01:16.939 --> 00:01:19.550
Derek: Depression is damaging and associated
with emotional distancing and

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:21.550
dysfunctional peer and family relationships.

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:24.829
Drug and alcohol abuse may be used to cope,
leading to life-long consequences.

00:01:24.829 --> 00:01:28.750
Derek: Tragically, due to its association
with suicide, depression can also be fatal.

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:32.671
Hanson: Screening for depression, whether
from a written PHQ-9 test or a

00:01:32.671 --> 00:01:37.130
psychiatrist-conducted psychological exam,
is important as a professional diagnosis

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:41.720
increases a patient’s access to rehabilitative
resources and the chance of recovery.

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:45.890
Natasha: Despite its severity, there is still
a negative societal stigma surrounding

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:50.600
depression, resulting in undermining and belittling
those who suffer from it.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:53.210
Increasing
awareness may alleviate this stigma, improving

00:01:53.210 --> 00:02:01.430
the wellbeing of students and citizens
worldwide.

